===Adverb===
{{en-adv}}

# In an [[accurate]] manner; exactly; [[precisely]]; without [[error]] or [[defect]].
#* {{quote-journal|en|author=Michael Snyder|title=A Guide to Guadalajara, Mexico’s City of Makers|magazine=w:The New York Times Style Magazine|url=https://www.nytimes.com/2023/11/17/t-magazine/locals-guide-guadalajara-mexico.html|date=2023-11-17|passage=For much of the 20th century, the image of Mexico popularized abroad through film, music, art and literature was, more '''accurately''', a portrayal of Jalisco state and especially its capital, Guadalajara.|archiveurl=https://archive.ph/Zam8s|archivedate=2023-11-17}}
#* {{quote-web|en|author=Evelynn Kersting|title=GAMES AND TIME|url=https://minds.wisconsin.edu/handle/1793/93321|url2=https://minds.wisconsin.edu/bitstream/handle/1793/93321/Kersting_uwm_0263D_13647.pdf|date=2023-12-01|archiveurl2=https://web.archive.org/web/20250606230955/https://minds.wisconsin.edu/bitstream/handle/1793/93321/Kersting_uwm_0263D_13647.pdf|page=11|work=w:University of Wisconsin-Milwaukee|passage=The internal NES clock must '''accurately''' measure down to milliseconds for its games to work properly.}}

